<title>FINLAND: NORDIC SKIING-WORLD CUP COMBINED LEADING RESULTS.</title>
<headline>NORDIC SKIING-WORLD CUP COMBINED LEADING RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>ROVANIEMI, Finland 1996-11-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading results in the ski-jumping leg of a Nordic combined World Cup event on Saturday:</p>
<p> 1.Jari Mantila		(Finland)  234.0 points (first jump</p>
<p>91.5 metres/second jump 91.5 metres)</p>
<p> 2.Mario Stecher	     (Austria)  224.5 points (87.0/91.0,</p>
<p>57 seconds behind)</p>
<p> 3.Tim Tetreault	     (U.S.)	224.0</p>
<p>(89.0/88.5, 1:00)</p>
<p> 4.Samppa Lajunen	    (Finland)  219.5</p>
<p>(88.0/90.0, 1:27)</p>
<p> 5.Fred B. Lundberg	  (Norway)   215.5</p>
<p>(85.0/89.0, 1:51)</p>
<p> 6.Kenji Ogiwara	     (Japan)    212.5</p>
<p>(84.5/88.0, 2:09)</p>
<p> 7 equal.Sylvain Guillaume (France)   212.0</p>
<p>(89.5/83.5, 2:12)</p>
<p> 7 equal.Toni Kilponen     (Finland)  212.0</p>
<p>(90.5/83.0, 2:12, behind)</p>
<p> 9.Halldor Skard	     (Norway)   211.0</p>
<p>(89.5/82.5, 2:18)</p>
<p>10.Kristian Hammer	   (Norway)   210.0</p>
<p>(82.5/89.5, 2:24)</p>
<p>(The second leg, a 15 km cross-country race, starts at 1005 GMT Sunday).</p>
